# Line endings are a repository property, not an author property.
#
# Every text file this repository governs is LF in the object database, so a
# diff shows the change and not the host that produced it. Without this file a
# CRLF checkout commits CRLF blobs and the next one-line edit renders as a
# whole-file diff (see #766: +349/-349 for a 10-line change).
#
# `text=auto` normalises on add. The explicit per-type lines are redundant for
# the object database but make the intent readable and survive `text=auto`
# being turned off for a path by a later rule.

* text=auto

*.rs   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

# --- One path gets a union merge driver, and only one ----------------------
#
# `14-ai-development/work-items/INDEX.md` is a table with one row per work
# item, and every registration appends a row. Two concurrent registrations
# therefore conflict on text adjacency alone, with no semantic disagreement:
# both rows are wanted, and nothing sorts the table. Measured on this file's
# own history: 61 rows added, 45 inserted mid-table and 16 at the end, so the
# conflict is not an EOF-append edge case (#1069).
#
# `merge=union` keeps both sides' added lines and resolves that shape with no
# human. It is exactly wrong for prose, which is why the rule is this path and
# not `*.md`.
#
# What union does NOT do, and what the resolver must know: it de-duplicates
# identical lines and keeps BOTH variants of a disagreeing one. So an edit to a
# row present on both sides yields two rows with one AID, and a deletion whose
# neighbouring line was edited on the other side comes back. All three silent
# failures end as the same AID on two lines, which is why the duplicate
# detector has to run before this driver can be trusted:
#
#   .github/workflows/repository-hygiene.yml
#     -> python3 scripts/check_traceability.py --index-only
#        -> T-04 duplicate INDEX entry {aid}
#
# If that step is removed or made advisory, delete this line in the same
# change. Without it, union converts a visible conflict into an invisible
# duplicate row, which is strictly worse than the conflict (#1064, #1071).

14-ai-development/work-items/INDEX.md merge=union

